# deskkey.ps2 - the keyboard leg of the event loop.
#
# `desk` polls the window's keyboard with SS.Ready and reads one byte only
# when it says there is one, so the loop stays responsive; `q` quits.  This
# script taps one key and nothing else, and the bench gives desk an iteration
# bound it could not possibly reach inside the run - so DESK-BYE arriving at
# all is the keystroke, and not the bound.
#
# ⚠ The key goes to the window CoArm has SELECTED (armio.asm routes it by
# VG.CSel), which is desk's; the shell's own standard input is the serial
# port and never sees it.  That separation is the whole reason a desktop can
# be driven from the keyboard while a shell waits on the same machine.
origin 320 240

at 1.500    key tap q
